# Test fixture (PRIZMO format): CIE hydrogen plus a He++ recombination whose
# rate is overridden by chemRate2() in the sibling react_cie_hepp.jfunc.
#
# chemRate2() returns n_Hejj (the He++ number density).  After the j/k charge
# convention migration, that symbol must decode to nden[<He++ index>, 0], so
# reaction index 2's rate ends up carrying the He++ density MatrixElement.

# idx 0: collisional ionization (Cen 1992)
H + E -> H+ + E + E   []   5.85e-11*sqrt(Tgas)*exp(-157809.1/Tgas)

# idx 1: hydrogen recombination
H+ + E -> H   []   2.6e-13*(Tgas/1e4)**(-0.8)

# idx 2: He++ recombination -- rate supplied by chemRate2() in the .jfunc
He++ + E -> He+   []   1.0
